      "The line chart illustrates the changes in the gross enrolment ratio in higher education in China from 1990 to 2019. As is clearly shown, the figure witnessed a steady and remarkable upward trend over these three decades. In 1990, only 3.4% of the eligible population entered higher education. This proportion climbed steadily, passing 11% in 2000 and 30% in 2012, before finally reaching 51.6% in 2019, roughly fifteen times the initial level.",
